	<item>
		<title>Orange Crush announces relaunch of Mid-South Wrestling</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398232-orange-crush-announces-relaunch-of-mid-south-wrestling/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398232-orange-crush-announces-relaunch-of-mid-south-wrestling/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:38:08 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Misc. News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[independent wrestling]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Mid-South Wrestling]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Orange Crush]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Produce Wrestling]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Razor Pro Wrestling]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398232</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In a statement released to the press on November 23, Orange Crush has announced the relaunch of Mid-South&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398232-orange-crush-announces-relaunch-of-mid-south-wrestling/">Orange Crush announces relaunch of Mid-South Wrestling</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In a statement released to the press on November 23, Orange Crush has announced the relaunch of Mid-South Wrestling, the result of a new partnership between PRODUCE and Razor Pro Wrestling to kick off in February 2027:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>FAYETTEVILLE, Ark. (November 23, 2026)</strong> — Razor Pro Wrestling and PRODUCE Wrestling today announced the launch of Mid-South Wrestling, a new promotion built on the legacy of one of professional wrestling’s best-known regional territories. Its first event takes place Sunday, February 21, 2027, at Ozark Music Hall in Fayetteville, Arkansas, with further events planned across Arkansas, Oklahoma, Missouri and Texas.<br><br>Mid-South Wrestling will be led locally by Ben Brecheen of Razor Pro Wrestling, in partnership with PRODUCE Wrestling and Adam Abdalla, founder of Orange Crush. Together, the two companies will bring leading independent and national talent back to the regional territories.<br><br>“Razor Pro and PRODUCE are collaborating to bring the best wrestling in the world back to the territories. We want to put on a top quality show where the world’s best tangle with future legends of the Mid-South region.” Abdalla continued “there are 40,000 college students in Fayetteville at the University of Arkansas. Let’s make &#8217;em proud wrestling fans. Woo Pig Sooie” said Adam Abdalla, founder of Orange Crush and PRODUCE Wrestling.<br><br>“With Razor Pro, we wanted to do something different. We set out to showcase the best from the region and put them in the ring with some of the best talent from around the country. I saw what Adam was doing with PRODUCE and he saw what I was doing at Razor Pro, and we became fast friends with similar visions.”<br><br>Brecheen continued, “the Southern territories always integrated star athletes, rock’n’roll stars, and world class professional wrestling into a modern presentation. We want to bring that back. Inspired by Bill Watts’ Mid-South, Crockett Promotions and the Jarretts, we want to bring together history, local pride, and wild ass fights. So much talent that came out of this territory along with a lot of rich history so we decided we should try to bring that magic back while respecting the past and accepting the present.” said Ben Brecheen of Razor Pro Wrestling.<br><br>The first confirmed names for the February 21 event are:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>AEW’s Adam Priest</li>



<li>AEW’s Bryan Keith</li>



<li>Paul Walter Hauser</li>



<li>Jonathan Gresham</li>



<li>Steve Maclin</li>



<li>Cappuccino Jones</li>



<li>Marko Stunt</li>



<li>Darian Bengston</li>



<li>Oni King</li>



<li>Effy</li>



<li>Kody Lane</li>



<li>Gringo Loco</li>



<li>K-Toomer</li>



<li>“Hot Sauce” Tracy Williams</li>



<li>Tim Bosby</li>



<li>Anna Ray</li>



<li>Aura Wisdom</li>



<li>Charli Evans</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br>Additional talent will be announced in the coming weeks.<br><br>The launch follows PRODUCE Wrestling’s 2026 season, which included shows curated by Jonathan Gresham, Lee Moriarty, Rocky Romero and The Dogs, and debuts in New York, Los Angeles and Montreal. Appearances included Zack Sabre Jr., Fuminori Abe, Kazuchika Okada, Lio Rush, Jeff Cobb, Hechicero, Minoru Suzuki, Tiger Mask, Black Tiger, Gabe Kidd, Clark Connors, David Finlay, Persephone, The Amazing Red, Low Ki and Karl Greco-Malenko, among others.<br><br><br><strong>Event Details</strong><br><strong>What</strong>: Mid-South Wrestling launch event<br><strong>When</strong>: Sunday, February 21, 2027, Doors: 1pm /Bell Time: 2pm<br><strong>Where</strong>: Ozark Music Hall, Fayetteville, Arkansas<br><strong>Tickets</strong>: Available Now: <a href="https://us.list-manage.com/ii5aoynAm4g?e=2c91a53a09&amp;c2id=c644ffd6d9895201f6fd668d7da3055d" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://stubs.net/event/8402/<wbr>mid-south-wrestling-vol-1</a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398232-orange-crush-announces-relaunch-of-mid-south-wrestling/">Orange Crush announces relaunch of Mid-South Wrestling</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/398232-orange-crush-announces-relaunch-of-mid-south-wrestling/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>WWE Hall of Famer&#8217;s WrestleMania 18 boot sells for over $400K on auction</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398202-wwe-hall-of-famers-wrestlemania-18-boot-sells-for-over-400k-on-auction/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398202-wwe-hall-of-famers-wrestlemania-18-boot-sells-for-over-400k-on-auction/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:22:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[collectible]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Hulk Hogan]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WrestleMania 18]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[wrestling boot]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398202</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Following the sale of Hulk Hogan&#8217;s left boot from WrestleMania 18, the right boot has now found a&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398202-wwe-hall-of-famers-wrestlemania-18-boot-sells-for-over-400k-on-auction/">WWE Hall of Famer&#8217;s WrestleMania 18 boot sells for over $400K on auction</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Following the sale of Hulk Hogan&#8217;s left boot from WrestleMania 18, the right boot has now found a new home following an auction this past weekend.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The boot, signed by the late WWE Hall of Famer, was authenticated by Beckett and listed by Goldin collectibles.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The boot, custom made by J&amp;M Custom Boots for Hogan&#8217;s match against The Rock, sold for $494,100 in the auction that began last month, coming out at $405,000 after the buyer&#8217;s premium.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hogan&#8217;s left boot sold for significantly less at an auction earlier this year, with the winning bid coming in at $146,400.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Final Sale Price on this Hulk Hogan WrestleMania X8 (18) Match-Used, Photo-Matched, Signed, Inscribed Right Boot vs. Dwayne &quot;The Rock&quot; Johnson: $494,100<br><br>Email us at Sell@Goldin.com to consign your Combat Sports Memorabilia to one of our upcoming Elite Auctions! <a href="https://t.co/BIIwTzMlGl">pic.twitter.com/BIIwTzMlGl</a></p>&mdash; Goldin (@GoldinCo) <a href="https://x.com/GoldinCo/status/2124755521638994273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 23, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398202-wwe-hall-of-famers-wrestlemania-18-boot-sells-for-over-400k-on-auction/">WWE Hall of Famer&#8217;s WrestleMania 18 boot sells for over $400K on auction</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398202-wwe-hall-of-famers-wrestlemania-18-boot-sells-for-over-400k-on-auction/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>WWE Raw Results &#8211; 11/23/26 (Roman Reigns and The Bloodline appear, final build to Survivor Series)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/398196-wwe-raw-results-november-23-2026-wichita/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/398196-wwe-raw-results-november-23-2026-wichita/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Mike Tedesco]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:57:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE RAW Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[2026]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Kansas]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[live results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[live WWE results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[November 23]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Wichita]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398196</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>WWE Raw ResultsNovember 23, 2026Wichita, Kansas (Intrust Bank Arena)Commentary: Michael Cole and Corey GravesResults by: Mike Tedesco of&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/398196-wwe-raw-results-november-23-2026-wichita/">WWE Raw Results &#8211; 11/23/26 (Roman Reigns and The Bloodline appear, final build to Survivor Series)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<figure class="wp-block-image is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="207" height="112" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/image-21.png" alt="" class="wp-image-375213" style="aspect-ratio:1.8482142857142858;width:207px;height:auto"/></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Raw Results<br>November 23, 2026<br>Wichita, Kansas (Intrust Bank Arena)<br>Commentary: Michael Cole and Corey Graves<br>Results by: Mike Tedesco of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;Then. Now. Forever. Together.&#8221; The WWE video leads us into the show.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go live from Intrust Bank Arena to see&nbsp;<strong>The 946</strong>&nbsp;viciously beating&nbsp;the <strong>Alpha Academy</strong>. The Alpha Academy had just finished a match that was taped for WWE Main Event when The 946 attacked. Cruz Montana gives Akira Tozawa a back suplex onto the commentary table. Bronco Nima and Lucien Price give Otis a double-team Samoan Drop. Carmelo Hayes grabs a microphone and says the Alpha Academy are trash.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Royce Keys sits uninterestedly in the ring as The 946 gather around him. Hayes says The Bloodline is watching what&#8217;s happening as they sit on Roman Reigns&#8217; bus. That&#8217;s the difference between them. The Bloodline thrives on comfort, but The 946 thrives on adversity and struggle. That&#8217;ll always be the difference. The crowd starts to loudly boo. Hayes says no one has ever challenged The Bloodline like them. They&#8217;ve bled all over the place. There are sharks and piranhas. They want everything on The Bloodline&#8217;s plate. At WarGames, they&#8217;ll realize that blood isn&#8217;t thicker than mud. At Survivor Series, The Bloodline will acknowledge them.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nima says they&#8217;re more than just a family. The same pressures that bend and break you are the same ones they carry on their shoulders. No one feels The 946. Price says you&#8217;re either with them or against them. An &#8220;OTC&#8221; chant fires up. Price says they&#8217;re here to get paid, so you either lay down or get down because today&#8217;s price isn&#8217;t yesterday&#8217;s price.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Montana says some of them have fought for their lives for the opportunity they have today. Now that they have it in their grasp, there&#8217;s no one alive who can take it from them. They&#8217;ve gone through life having to make something from nothing, so they&#8217;ve got to squeeze it for everything it&#8217;s got. They&#8217;re at war. At Survivor Series, The Bloodline will pay in blood.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Another &#8220;OTC&#8221; chant fires up. The 946 gathers around Keys. Keys says Roman Reigns is a rich, wealthy man. He&#8217;s the Big Dog, the Tribal Chief, and the OTC. All this started because of what he told Jacob Fatu to do to him. What&#8217;d Reigns tell him? That Keys isn&#8217;t family, blood, or Bloodline. He&#8217;s just one of the boys. Keys says he&#8217;s got his boys now. People like them jump into the deep end and swim with the sharks. At Survivor Series, they&#8217;ll take out Reigns&#8217; Bloodline. Then, Keys is coming for the grand prize. He&#8217;s coming after Reigns. Jaida Parker takes the microphone and says, &#8220;Ain&#8217;t nobody safe.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This Saturday, The 946 battles The Bloodline in a WarGames Match at Survivor Series.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Strong start to <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a>. I like when they start with some chaos to pull you in quickly. The show is so formulaic that whenever they break the flow even a little bit, it feels very fresh. Great stuff to keep building The 946. I&#39;m interested to see how <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SurvivorSeries?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SurvivorSeries</a> turns out.</p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2125005203254731102?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 23, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Later tonight, we&#8217;ll hear from World Heavyweight Champion Roman Reigns. Teams USA and Mexico will announce their fifth members tonight.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Pre-Show Arrivals</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Stephanie Vaquer and Sol Ruca are shown arriving.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Intercontinental Champion &#8220;All Ego&#8221; Ethan Page</strong> makes his entrance. He puts the title on the line against AAA World Cruiserweight Champion Rey Fénix next.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<h3 id="wwe-intercontinental-championshipall-ego-ethan-page-c-vs-aaa-world-cruiserweight-champion-rey-fenix" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>WWE Intercontinental Championship</strong><br>“All Ego” Ethan Page (c) vs. AAA World Cruiserweight Champion Rey Fénix</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Rod Zapata</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fénix ducks a lock-up and hooks a side headlock. Page whips him off and shoulder tackles him down before posing. Fénix kips up and gets in his face. Page sends him into the ropes, but Fénix ducks a clothesline and hits a running hurricanrana, followed by a dropkick that sends him out of the ring. As Page gets back into the ring, Fénix hits him with a rolling thunder hurricanrana for a near fall! Page rolls out of the ring and avoids a baseball slide. Page attacks Fénix as he slides into the ring and punches away at his skull. Page sends Fénix into the ropes for a back elbow to the jaw. Fénix punches Page as he approaches him. Page quickly knees him in the midsection to take him down. Page hits a backbreaker and takes a moment to collect himself. Fénix chops Page, but Page kicks him in the ribs. Fénix may have injured his wrist blocking the kick. Page lifts Fénix, but Fénix slides off and rocks him with a pair of superkicks. Page is stunned against the ropes. Fénix goes to the top rope for Adios, Amigo, but Page shakes the ropes, knocking him to the floor!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Picture-in-Picture Commercial Break:</strong> Page keeps the advantage over Fénix, driving him into the barricade and the ring apron before getting him into the ring. Fénix responds with some chops and rebounds off the ropes before stunning Page with a superkick. Fénix backs up, gets the crowd going, then charges in for a double knee strike to the face. Both men are down. Fénix is still holding his wrist in pain. Page forearms Fénix in the jaw and chops him in the corner. Page puts Fénix on the top rope and climbs to the second rope. Page attacks Fénix and taunts the crowd.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fénix elbows away at Page to avoid a slam off the top rope. Fénix then hits a wild super hurricanrana and follows up with a massive low-down frog splash! 1… 2… Page kicks out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fénix grabs Page, shakes off a strike, and superkicks him. Fénix goes for a handspring cutter, but Page sidesteps it before hitting a powerslam for a near fall. Page sets up for an Ego-Plex, but Fénix counters into an inside cradle for a near fall. Page pops up and immediately connects with a big boot for a two-count.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The crowd is chanting for Fénix. Page puts Fénix on the top rope, but Fénix slips down and hits him with a powerbomb off the second rope. Fénix sets up for a rolling cutter, but Page superkicks him. Page pushes Fénix into the ropes, but he hits a handspring cutter. Fénix goes to the corner and hits a rolling thunder cutter for a near fall!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Michael Cole says this is an incredible match to kick off Friday Night SmackDown. Oops. Page rolls out of the ring, so Fénix CRUSHES him with a suicide dive somersault plancha. Fénix gets Page into the ring and goes to the top rope, but Page rolls to the floor. Fénix spins and hits a BEAUTIFUL moonsault block to the floor! Fénix gets Page in the ring and hits a running kick in the corner. Fénix sets up for a Mexican Muscle Buster, but Page rips at his mask. The referee warns Page. Page attacks Fénix from behind and hits an Ego-Plex for the victory.</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-pinfall-and-still-wwe-intercontinental-champion-all-ego-ethan-page" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by Pinfall and still WWE Intercontinental Champion: “All Ego” Ethan Page</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Very good match with Ethan Page and Rey Fénix. Fénix is always great, but Page looked particularly good here. The guy is good with the right opponent. I was a little worried that Fénix tweaked his wrist. He was holding it all match, but he seems fine. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2125009884869492996?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 23, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Replay:</strong> <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-smackdown-results/398035-wwe-smackdown-results-11-20-26-wargames-advantage-match/">This past Friday on SmackDown</a>, Damian Priest took WWE United States Champion Trick Williams out with a ring bell shot. Williams will not be able to compete at Survivor Series, which removes him from Team USA.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Hall of Famer Rey Mysterio</strong> heads to the ring. We&#8217;ll hear from the captain of Team Mexico next.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<h3 id="rey-mysterio-addresses-who-the-fifth-member-of-team-mexico-is" class="wp-block-heading">Rey Mysterio addresses who the fifth member of Team Mexico is</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Hall of Famer Rey Mysterio </strong>is in the ring. Team USA vs. Team Mexico will be unlike anything you&#8217;ve seen before. To USA&#8217;s credit, their team is stacked. They have LA Knight, Je&#8217;Von Evans, CM Punk, and Cody Rhodes as Team Captain. As captain of Team Mexico, Mysterio can say with pride that he has picked the very best that Mexico has to offer. That is himself, Dragon Lee, Rey Fénix, Penta with zero miedo, and&#8230; Mysterio says he could say the wait is over and Team Mexico is now complete because he&#8217;s going to announce the fifth member of Team Mexico. That is&#8230;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>&#8220;Dirty&#8221; Dominik Mysterio</strong> heads to the ring with <strong>JD McDonagh</strong>. Rey shakes his head in anger. McDonagh tells the crowd to shut up and show Dominik some respect. This is a son trying to repair his relationship with his father. Dominik calls Rey, &#8220;Dad,&#8221; something he hasn&#8217;t done in years. Dominik and McDonagh get into the ring. Dominik says he knows his father may have found a fifth member, but he wants to say one thing. Dominik wanted to join Team USA, but after talking to &#8220;that bum&#8221; LA Knight and &#8220;Captain Crybaby,&#8221; Dominik realized that the blood that runs through his veins is Mexican. McDonagh shouts, &#8220;Viva la raza!&#8221; Dominik says he understands they&#8217;ve had their differences over the years over the way Rey treated him growing up. Dominik is willing to let bygones be bygones and start over if Rey stops playing around and adds him to Team Mexico. The crowd loudly boos.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rey looks at his son and says he&#8217;s touched by what Dominik said. It sounds like it came from the heart. Rey says he&#8217;s building a team of luchadores, not trust fund jackasses. Rey goes to announce the fifth member, but Dominik stops him and says he&#8217;s the King of the Luchadores. There is no luchador better than Dominik Mysterio. Rey says there is. If Rey says, &#8220;El Grande Americano,&#8221; he&#8217;ll lose his mind. Dominik says it better not be him. Rey asks if he&#8217;ll be quiet so he can announce the fifth member of Team Mexico. Dominik says Americano is a disgrace and not a real Mexican. Rey announces El Grande Americano as the fifth member of Team Mexico.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>AAA Mega Champion El Grande Americano</strong> makes his entrance to a big ovation. Dominik is infuriated. Americano greets the crowd and says he&#8217;s the fifth and final member of Team Mexico. He calls Dominik a &#8220;cabron.&#8221; In his heart, Americano is much more Mexican than Dominik. To prove that, he spoke with Adam Pearce. Tonight, it&#8217;ll be The Judgment Day vs. Rey Mysterio and El Grande Americano right here and now! The crowd loudly cheers.</p>



<h3 id="tag-team-matchwwe-hall-of-famer-rey-mysterio-and-aaa-mega-champion-el-grande-americano-vs-the-judgment-day-dirty-dominik-mysterio-and-jd-mcdonagh" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Tag Team Match</strong><br>WWE Hall of Famer Rey Mysterio and AAA Mega Champion El Grande Americano vs. The Judgment Day (&#8220;Dirty&#8221; Dominik Mysterio and JD McDonagh)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Danilo Anfibio</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">McDonagh and Dominik immediately blindside Rey and Americano, stomping away at him. Americano fights back as McDonagh takes Rey down with a drop toehold and drops a leg. McDonagh knees Rey and sends him into the ropes for a tilt-a-whirl backbreaker, but Rey counters out and drops him into position. Dominik pulls McDonagh out of the way of a 619. Americano hits McDonagh with a suicide dive. Rey then follows up with a flying seated senton off the apron onto Dominik.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Americano shoulder tackles McDonagh and sends him into the ropes for a dropkick. Americano hits an arm drag and applies an armbar. McDonagh fights up and hits a jawbreaker. McDonagh chops Americano, but Americano chops him back. Americano hits a textbook vertical suplex for a two-count. Americano whips McDonagh to the opposite corner, but McDonagh twists out of the way and takes him down. McDonagh hits a slingshot corkscrew plancha for a two-count. McDonagh rips at Americano&#8217;s mask before tagging Dominik in. The Judgment Day sends Americano into the ropes, but he breaks up a double-team attempt.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rey tags in and punches away at Dominik. Dominik reverses a whip, but Rey comes back with a head-scissor takeover. Rey gets the crowd going and shoulders Dominik in the corner. Rey climbs the ropes, but Dominik pulls him down. Dominik sends him to the opposite corner and counters a slingshot with an Alabama Slam attempt. Rey slides out and knocks him into position, but Dominik responds with a superkick. Dominik sends Rey into the ropes, but he holds on and boots Dominik back. Rey then clotheslines McDonagh off the apron. Dominik attacks his father from behind and tags McDonagh in. McDonagh hits Rey with a slingshot moonsault, landing on Rey&#8217;s face. Dominik tags in and hits a slingshot somersault senton before knocking Americano off the apron. Dominik punches and stomps away at his father for a two-count. Dominik puts Rey on the top rope and hits some crossfaces before pulling him into the tree of woe. Dominik dropkicks Rey in the midsection and covers for a two-count.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We return from the break to see Rey fighting McDonagh away. McDonagh scoops Rey up, but Rey slides off and hits a jawbreaker. McDonagh quickly stops Rey from making a tag. Rey kicks McDonagh away. Dominik tags in and stops his father from making a tag. Dominik starts up the Three Amigos. 1 Amigo&#8230; 2 Amigos&#8230; and 3 Amigos. McDonagh tags in and drops an elbow before taunting the crowd. Rey starts fighting back, elbows McDonagh, then goes for a springboard moonsault block. McDonagh catches him and tries to slam him, but Rey (sort of) counters with a DDT. McDonagh gets up and lifts him for a vertical suplex, but Rey firmly plants him with a DDT to counter out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Americano and Dominik tag in. Americano punches Dominik and McDonagh down. Americano hits Dominik with a back body drop, followed by a rolling Death Valley Driver to McDonagh. Americano hits Dominik with an Air Raid Crash for a near fall. Americano gets the crowd going and goes to the top rope, but McDonagh crotches him. Outside the ring, Rey attacks McDonagh, but McDonagh sends him into the ring post. In the ring, Dominik tags McDonagh as he comes off the top rope with a Frog Splash. McDonagh follows up with a moonsault for a near fall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Dominik tags in and dropkicks Americano into position. Americano avoids a 619, and Rey drops McDonagh into position. Rey hits Dominik and McDonagh with a double 619. Rey then catches McDonagh with a wild hurricanrana over the top rope. Americano then smashes Dominik with an Aztec Headbutt for the win.</p>



<h3 id="winners-by-pinfall-wwe-hall-of-famer-rey-mysterio-and-aaa-mega-champion-el-grande-americano" class="wp-block-heading">Winners by Pinfall: WWE Hall of Famer Rey Mysterio and AAA Mega Champion El Grande Americano</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Terrific tag team match with Rey Mysterio and El Grande Americano going over &quot;Dirty&quot; Dom and JD McDonagh. They gave this time, and it was very good. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2125019622856622426?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 24, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Still, I have to say, at this time last year, Dominik Mysterio was beating John Cena in his final PLE match. What has WWE done except lower his stock in the year since after being given the gift of a lifetime? And don&#39;t get me started about what they&#39;ve done with Gunther. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2125019895482003512?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 24, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Video:</strong> Agents of Shadows on ReelShort trailer.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Danhausen </strong>is hanging up signs for his Friendsgiving Party. <strong>&#8220;The American Nightmare&#8221; Cody Rhodes</strong> walks by him and knocks on a door. <strong>CM Punk</strong> comes out wearing American flag face paint. Punk is carrying &#8220;Hacksaw&#8221; Jim Duggan&#8217;s 2&#215;4. Punk knocks on another door, and <strong>World Tag Team Champion Je&#8217;Von Evans</strong> comes out. Next is <strong>LA Knight</strong>, who says he isn&#8217;t ready. Luckily, his team has an American flag bandana for him.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Rock returns this Saturday at Survivor Series.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>30 Years of The Rock:</strong> In 2012 at WrestleMania 28, The Rock defeated John Cena in a match billed as &#8220;Once in a Lifetime.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Gorilla Position</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Team USA is standing in the Gorilla Position. CM Punk is fired up and wants Cody Rhodes&#8217; music played because he&#8217;s the Team Captain.</p>



<h3 id="team-usa-addresses-who-their-fifth-member-will-be" class="wp-block-heading">Team USA addresses who their fifth member will be</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Team USA, consisting of <strong>&#8220;The American Nightmare&#8221; Cody Rhodes</strong>, <strong>CM Punk</strong>, <strong>World Tag Team Champion Je&#8217;Von Evans</strong>, and <strong>LA Knight</strong>, head to the ring as a united front to Rhodes&#8217; theme song. The crowd gives them a big ovation and chants, &#8220;USA!&#8221; Evans waves the flag in the ring. Rhodes greets the Wichita crowd and asks what they want to talk about. The crowd again chants, &#8220;USA.&#8221; Rhodes says it&#8217;s time to reveal their fifth member.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Je&#8217;Von Evans cuts in, saying the crowd isn&#8217;t loud enough for him. Evans gets them fired up. Rhodes goes to speak, but Knight interjects and tells him to get to the announcement. Knight then asks Evans if he said, &#8220;Yerp.&#8221; Knight says there&#8217;s a lot of talent in the ring. Even if they had &#8220;Hacksaw&#8221; Jim Duggan, they&#8217;d still win. Knight has love for Mexico, but they&#8217;re going to get a star-splattered &#8220;kiester-kicking&#8221; courtesy of LA Knight. Now, who is the fifth guy?</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rhodes goes to speak, but he stops to ask if anyone has anything else to say. Punk thanks Rhodes because he&#8217;s had the weight of the industry on his shoulders. Every feud is personal from a Rogues Gallery of Douchebags he&#8217;s assembled. This is the most fun Punk has had since coming back. He knows Rhodes won&#8217;t let him down. Rhodes announces that the fifth member of Team USA is&#8230;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Seth &#8220;Freakin&#8221; Rollins</strong>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Punk is not happy and angrily stares at Rhodes. Rhodes looks unhappy. Punk leaves the ring and heads to the back as Rollins gets inside. Rollins smiles. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">They definitely have been putting the schmaltz on for this whole Team USA vs. Team Mexico thing, so it was nice to see a little real storyline work here. You knew it was going to be Seth Rollins after the tease on <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/SmackDown?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#SmackDown</a>. They did a good job with the reveal. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2125026860400570450?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 24, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Replay:</strong> Earlier tonight, The 946 viciously attacked Alpha Academy before Royce Keys said he&#8217;ll be coming after Roman Reigns after Survivor Series is over.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Video:</strong> <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/397741-live-wwe-raw-results-november-16-2026-raleigh/">Last week on Raw</a>, The 946 won the advantage inside WarGames after defeating The Usos.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Interview</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jackie Redmond is with <strong>WWE Women&#8217;s Intercontinental Champion IYO SKY</strong>. Before Sky can really say anything, <strong>Lyra Valkyria</strong> interrupts. <strong>Sol Ruca</strong> then walks up and tells Sky to get a front row seat to watch their match. In the background,<strong> Danhausen</strong> and <strong>&#8220;Hacksaw&#8221; Jim Duggan</strong> are putting up more Friendgiving flyers.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Sol Ruca</strong> makes her entrance.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A furious <strong>CM Punk</strong> is walking backstage when <strong>Cody Rhodes</strong> catches up with him. Punk isn&#8217;t happy with Seth Rollins joining Team USA. Punk will be there on Saturday, but he isn&#8217;t happy about it. <strong>Seth Rollins</strong> comes over gloating, and Punk storms off. Rollins asks Rhodes if the co-captain spot is open.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Women&#8217;s Intercontinental Champion IYO SKY</strong> heads to the ring to watch the next match.</p>



<h3 id="sol-ruca-vs-lyra-valkyria" class="wp-block-heading">Sol Ruca vs. Lyra Valkyria</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Jessika Carr</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">They lock up, and Valkyria takes her down for a one-count. Ruca does a handspring out of a snapmare and takes Valkyria down with a pair of clotheslines. Ruca spins her around and hits a facebuster. Ruca soon knocks her out of the ring and hits a springboard corkscrew plancha to the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back from the break, Valkyria is stretching out Ruca. Ruca fights up and punches away at Valkyria. Ruca superkicks her down. After a few moments, Ruca lands a strike combo, sending her into the corner. Valkyria blocks a German Suplex and elbows her to the apron. Ruca snaps her off the top rope and hits a springboard frog splash for a two-count. Valkyria fights back with a chop block. Valkyria hits a DDT, followed by a fisherman&#8217;s buster for a two-count. Ruca tries to fight back, but Valkyria blocks a German Suplex and hits a spin kick. Valkyria stares at Sky, and Ruca surprises her with a Sol Snatcher for the win.</p>



<h3 id="winner-by-pinfall-sol-ruca" class="wp-block-heading">Winner by Pinfall: Sol Ruca</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Not much of a match with Lyra Valkyria and Sol Ruca. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWERaw?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWERaw</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2125031698001723799?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 24, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Video:</strong> Women&#8217;s World Champion Liv Morgan says she&#8217;s taken everything she&#8217;s wanted, including &#8220;Dirty&#8221; Dominik Mysterio and The Judgment Day. While she was training, she watched Becky Lynch become The Man and the greatest of all time, so she took everything that was dear to Lynch. Now, with the help of Roxanne Perez, she&#8217;ll defeat Lynch once and for all. Perez says she can&#8217;t expect Lynch to understand loyalty to family. Morgan says she&#8217;ll continue to be the greatest Women&#8217;s World Champion of all time.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Video:</strong> Earlier today, <strong>&#8220;The Ruler&#8221; Oba Femi</strong> was confronted in the parking lot by <strong>The Vision</strong>. Before anything could happen, <strong>Raw General Manager Adam Pearce </strong>intervened.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Segment</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>&#8220;The Ruler&#8221; Oba Femi</strong> is shown walking. We&#8217;ll hear from him next.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Video:</strong> George Kittle of the San Francisco 49ers arrived at last night&#8217;s game in Mexico City wearing a Penta mask.</p>



<h3 id="the-ruler-oba-femi-addresses-the-vision" class="wp-block-heading">&#8220;The Ruler&#8221; Oba Femi addresses The Vision</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>&#8220;The Ruler&#8221; Oba Femi</strong>&nbsp;is heading to the ring, and he looks&nbsp;angry. Femi says that the ego of The Vision won&#8217;t allow them to let anything go. Femi hasn&#8217;t had a reason to eliminate them for good, but he&#8217;s getting past that. Femi gives them an ultimatum: stand down or he will show them why he is The Destroyer. Femi put down his last rival for good. Now, The Vision must stand down.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Video:</strong> Two weeks ago, The 946 attacked Chad Gable, Big Cass, and Dragon Lee.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Backstage Interview</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jackie Redmond is backstage with <strong>Chad Gable</strong>. Gable says he&#8217;s not going to let The 946 run roughshod through everyone because he&#8217;s got balls and guts. <strong>Big Cass</strong> walks up and taunts Gable. Gable challenges him to a match next week.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fatal Influence battles Stephanie Vaquer and Bayley next.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<h3 id="tag-team-matchfatal-influence-lainey-reid-and-fallon-henley-w-wwe-womens-united-states-champion-jacy-jayne-vs-bayley-and-stephanie-vaquer" class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Tag Team Match</strong><br>Fatal Influence (Lainey Reid and Fallon Henley) w/ WWE Women&#8217;s United States Champion Jacy Jayne vs. Bayley and Stephanie Vaquer</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Referee:</strong> Eddie Orengo</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bayley starts off with a Bayley-to-Belly on Lainey Reid. Henley fights out of it, but Bayley takes her down and tags in Stephanie Vaquer. Vaquer takes it to Henley before Bayley tags back in. Reid and Henley take her out as we go to commercial.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Refresh for the latest results.</em></p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<h3 id="quick-match-results" class="wp-block-heading">Quick Match Results</h3>



<p class="cnvs-block-core-paragraph-1795476585901 wp-block-paragraph">&#8212; &#8220;All Ego&#8221; Ethan Page (c) def. AAA World Cruiserweight Champion Rey Fénix to retain the WWE Intercontinental Championship<br>&#8212; WWE Hall of Famer Rey Mysterio and AAA Mega Champion El Grande Americano* def. The Judgment Day (&#8220;Dirty&#8221; Dominik Mysterio* and JD McDonagh) in a Tag Team Match<br>&#8212; Sol Ruca def. Lyra Valkyria</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/398196-wwe-raw-results-november-23-2026-wichita/">WWE Raw Results &#8211; 11/23/26 (Roman Reigns and The Bloodline appear, final build to Survivor Series)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-raw-results/398196-wwe-raw-results-november-23-2026-wichita/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews rules out a 2026 return, provides an update on WWE&#8217;s Rhea Ripley</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398187-aews-buddy-matthews-rules-out-a-2026-return-provides-an-update-on-wwes-rhea-ripley/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398187-aews-buddy-matthews-rules-out-a-2026-return-provides-an-update-on-wwes-rhea-ripley/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:33:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Buddy Matthews]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[recovery]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[return]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Rhea Ripley]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398187</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews spoke recently with &#8216;KingWins social casino&#8217; (https://kingwins.com) about a possible return before the end the&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398187-aews-buddy-matthews-rules-out-a-2026-return-provides-an-update-on-wwes-rhea-ripley/">AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews rules out a 2026 return, provides an update on WWE&#8217;s Rhea Ripley</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews spoke recently with &#8216;KingWins social casino&#8217; (<a href="https://kingwins.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://kingwins.com</a>) about a possible return before the end the year. In addition, he also provided an update on Rhea Ripley. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>On a possible return to the ring before the end of this year:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">“I&#8217;d say this year has gone so quickly. We&#8217;re going to be out of the year in the next four or five weeks, especially with the holidays coming up.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I don&#8217;t want to force it or rush anything. I&#8217;ve lost the better part of two years to this. When I return, I want it to mean something. I want it to be special, and I want it to be right.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">When I come back, I&#8217;m not coming back to do the same things I was doing before. I have two years to make up, so when I return, I&#8217;m coming back to leave a mark.”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>On the recovery status of Rhea Ripley:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">“She [Rhea Ripley] is doing well. This was probably the first surgery she&#8217;s ever had, so it caught her a little off guard. Her pain tolerance is like no other, and her work ethic puts me to shame.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">She puts anyone else to shame when it comes to work ethic. To actually see her have to stop and recover from something was new to both her and me.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">She&#8217;s getting there every day and getting stronger. She was in the gym 12 hours after surgery doing upper body. That 12 hours off was as long as she could go!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">She&#8217;s working really, really hard, and she&#8217;ll be back sooner rather than later too. When she comes back, she&#8217;s a one-of-one. She&#8217;s going to make a mark, and I feel wrestling is better with her in it.”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">****</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Matthews has been out of in-ring action since February 2025 due to an ankle injury. He was medically cleared this past August 2026. However, despite being cleared, he has not yet wrestled a match and was pulled from a planned appearance at the World Series Wrestling’s MEGAMANIA tour due to scheduling conflicts.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">His initial injury happened during AEW Grand Slam Australia 2025, having rolled his ankle during his ring entrance against Kazuchika Okada.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ripley, who is the real-life wife of Matthews, suffered a torn meniscus around during her WWE Women&#8217;s Championship defense against Jade Cargill at Clash in Italy back on May 31. Ripley underwent surgery in early August.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398187-aews-buddy-matthews-rules-out-a-2026-return-provides-an-update-on-wwes-rhea-ripley/">AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews rules out a 2026 return, provides an update on WWE&#8217;s Rhea Ripley</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398187-aews-buddy-matthews-rules-out-a-2026-return-provides-an-update-on-wwes-rhea-ripley/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews on how much longer he thinks he will wrestle, ambitions for when he finally returns to the ring &#124; EXCLUSIVE</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398179-aews-buddy-matthews-exclusive/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398179-aews-buddy-matthews-exclusive/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:19:23 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ambitions]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Buddy Matthews]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[return]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398179</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>I recently had an opportunity to speak exclusively with AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews on behalf of &#8216;KingWins social casino&#8217;&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398179-aews-buddy-matthews-exclusive/">AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews on how much longer he thinks he will wrestle, ambitions for when he finally returns to the ring | EXCLUSIVE</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I recently had an opportunity to speak exclusively with AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews on behalf of &#8216;KingWins social casino&#8217; (<a href="https://kingwins.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://kingwins.com</a>).</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>At 38 years old, how much longer do you think you want to continue wrestling? Do you have any ambitions for when you finally return to the ring?</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;I always say this to my wife. At the end of the day, even though I&#8217;m 38, I&#8217;m still 18 in my head.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I haven&#8217;t really changed. I&#8217;m the same guy I was when I first started, just with a lot more things I have to do every day.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;m still a kid.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you say another seven years, that takes me to 45, which is still pretty young. I feel young, and I definitely take care of my health.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Since I&#8217;ve been injured, I&#8217;ve been working on bringing my biological age down. I&#8217;m 38, but my biological age is 34, so I&#8217;m four years ahead of the pace. I&#8217;m doing okay there.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I don&#8217;t want to be 50 and still wrestling. I want to do good work and get out with my health intact. Hopefully, I&#8217;ll have a family, and then we can enjoy the fruits of our labour.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">My wife and I have lost a lot of time with our family since taking this venture. I&#8217;ve been over here for 13 years, and she&#8217;s been here for eight.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">That&#8217;s a lot of weddings, birthdays, moments and Christmases we&#8217;ve missed. We&#8217;ve sacrificed a lot for this life, and we&#8217;re very blessed to have it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">But we also want to be able to live it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One of the nice things about both of us being injured is that we&#8217;ve actually been able to spend time together.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;m not going to set a retirement date because then it&#8217;ll just get thrown in my face!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I don&#8217;t want to be doing this when I shouldn&#8217;t be doing it.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">****</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Matthews has been out of in-ring action since February 2025 due to an ankle injury. He was medically cleared this past August 2026. However, despite being cleared, he has not yet wrestled a match and was pulled from a planned appearance at the World Series Wrestling&#8217;s MEGAMANIA tour due to scheduling conflicts.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">His initial injury happened during AEW Grand Slam Australia 2025, having rolled his ankle during his ring entrance against Kazuchika Okada.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398179-aews-buddy-matthews-exclusive/">AEW&#8217;s Buddy Matthews on how much longer he thinks he will wrestle, ambitions for when he finally returns to the ring | EXCLUSIVE</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398179-aews-buddy-matthews-exclusive/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
