		<item>
		<title>Update on the status of Mark Briscoe&#8217;s absence from AEW TV</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398169-update-on-the-status-of-mark-briscoes-absence-from-aew-tv/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398169-update-on-the-status-of-mark-briscoes-absence-from-aew-tv/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:00:16 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Mark Briscoe]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[update]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398169</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Fightful Select has published an update on the status of Mark Briscoe, who has been absent from AEW&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398169-update-on-the-status-of-mark-briscoes-absence-from-aew-tv/">Update on the status of Mark Briscoe&#8217;s absence from AEW TV</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fightful Select has published an update on the status of Mark Briscoe, who has been absent from AEW TV since the July 1 episode of Dynamite, where he was unsuccessful in capturing the World Title from then champion MJF.  </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">According to the report, Briscoe has been recovering from a knee injury which required surgery.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fightful also notes Briscoe&#8217;s surgery reportedly was done during his time away from the ring. There were no specific details given regarding the procedure. At the time of the report, there is no confirmed timeline as to when Briscoe will return to AEW television. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Specific details regarding the procedure have not been disclosed, and there is currently no confirmed timetable for his return to AEW programming.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398169-update-on-the-status-of-mark-briscoes-absence-from-aew-tv/">Update on the status of Mark Briscoe&#8217;s absence from AEW TV</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398169-update-on-the-status-of-mark-briscoes-absence-from-aew-tv/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW star provides update on shoulder surgery recovery</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398166-aew-star-provides-update-on-shoulder-surgery-recovery/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398166-aew-star-provides-update-on-shoulder-surgery-recovery/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:45:08 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Anna Jay]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[surgery]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[update]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398166</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW star Anna Jay provided an update on her recovery from shoulder surgery. During her recent Twitch stream,&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398166-aew-star-provides-update-on-shoulder-surgery-recovery/">AEW star provides update on shoulder surgery recovery</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">AEW star Anna Jay provided an update on her recovery from shoulder surgery.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During her recent <a href="https://www.twitch.tv/videos/2935661705" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Twitch stream</a>, Jay said her shoulder is doing good and that her doctor said it is healing good. Jay also said that she is no longer needs to use a sling.  Jay further noted that she is doing physical therapy several times a week. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>“Yes, the shoulder is doing good. It’s going as it should. I saw my doctor at six weeks as well…he said everything looked good and is healing good, so that is great.  I’m going two to three times a week. I think I’ve said this, but for everyone who’s listening now &#8211; it’s kicking my a&#8211;. It’s hard. You know, I’ve had the labrum shoulder surgery, that was not as tough. This one is pretty rough, to be honest…it’s rough, but it’s a good rough because this is supposed to mean that it’s in there. It’s screwed in with two screws. No one’s messing with me.”</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jay last wrestled on the June 6 episode of AEW Collision, when she teamed up with Tay Melo, where they were unsuccessful in capturing the AEW Women&#8217;s World Tag Team Titles against then champions Divine Dominion.  Jay signed a contract extension with AEW back in July.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398166-aew-star-provides-update-on-shoulder-surgery-recovery/">AEW star provides update on shoulder surgery recovery</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/398166-aew-star-provides-update-on-shoulder-surgery-recovery/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
